stdout | Eqwalize all opted-in modules in specified buck target
stdout |
stdout | Usage: elp eqwalize-target [OPTIONS] <TARGET>
stdout |
stdout | Arguments:
stdout |   <TARGET>  target, like //erl/chatd/...
stdout |
stdout | Options:
stdout |       --project <PROJECT>  Path to directory with project, or to a JSON file [default: .]
stdout |       --format <FORMAT>    Customize the output format (defaults to human-readable) [possible
stdout |                            values: json]
stdout |       --connect            Use the persistent daemon for fast turnaround (default when watchman is
stdout |                            installed; auto-starts if needed). Pass --no-connect to disable
stdout |       --no-connect         Disable the persistent daemon and run standalone (no cross-run caching)
stdout |       --bail-on-error      Exit with a non-zero status code if any errors are found
stdout |   -h, --help               Print help
stdout |
stdout | Global options:
stdout |       --log-file <LOG_FILE>  
stdout |       --erl <ERL>            
stdout |       --escript <ESCRIPT>    
stdout |       --no-log-buffering     
stdout |       --no-buck-generated    Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
stdout |       --buck-quick-start     Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
stdout |       --color <WHEN>         Use color in output [default: always] [possible values: always, never,
stdout |                              auto]
